    "created_at": "2021-11-17T12:21:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-17T12:21:17Z",
    "body": "> it can cover up the end of the password if you don't account for it being there\r\n\r\nThat's not what I'm seeing.  The scroll box for the text value ends at the edge of the button, as expected.  What sometimes happens in Edge though is when you toggle between the masked/unmasked values the scroll position unexpectedly moves so that the end of the value is scrolled out of view. This seems to happen when the characters are wider than the \"bullet\" characters used for the masking. I tested with characters that are the same width (or narrower) such as \"i\" and \"I\" then the end of the value stays visible when toggling between masked/unmasked.  I think what you're describing is just a bug in Edge.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
