    "created_at": "2021-12-07T18:54:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-07T18:54:18Z",
    "body": "Safari already presents some UI inside `<input type=password>` for autofill. It would be challenging to also squeeze in some other UI while retaining usability, especially on small form fields. I'd generally prefer the spec not mandate UI here.\r\n\r\nMaybe the spec could say something like \"IF the UA exposes its own UI for this, that UI MUST be implemented by setting the `input-security` property on the element.\" That way we could at least ensure browser-provided UI and page-provided UI didn't fight each other.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
