    "created_at": "2023-07-15T04:09:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-15T04:09:44Z",
    "body": "The compat spec is really here to describe things which need to be implemented when there is no spec for them. Aka browsers **have to implement** them to be compatible with the Web. And very often it should be only a transitory specification until there's a right place for the feature to be specified. \r\n\r\nin the case of `::-ms-reveal`, do other browsers need to implement this to be compatible with the Web? Aka do websites stop working if it's not in Firefox, Safari and Chrome? ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
